# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 7.2 — isolated test environment.
#
# Loaded ONLY when NODE_ENV=test, by `scripts/load-test-env.cjs`, which runs as
# the first `--import` of every test command. It is applied with override
# semantics and is therefore applied BEFORE the `import 'dotenv/config'` in
# `src/lib/env.ts` and `test/helpers.ts`. dotenv does not overwrite values that
# are already present in `process.env`, so `.env` (which points at production)
# can never win over this file.
#
# There are NO real credentials here and none are needed:
#   * PostgreSQL/Redis are disposable Docker containers bound to non-default
#     ports on loopback only (see `npm run test:db:up`).
#   * TYPESENSE_*, GEMINI_API_KEY and YOUTUBE_API_KEY are inert local
#     placeholders. Nothing in the test suite is allowed to reach a third party;
#     tests that exercise an HTTP client stub `fetch`.
#
# Because this file contains no secret, it is deliberately NOT gitignored (see
# `.gitignore`) so CI and every contributor get the same isolation contract.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_ENV=test

# ─── Disposable data stores (loopback, non-default ports) ───────────────────
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://afrogenie:afrogenie@localhost:55432/afrogenie?schema=public
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://afrogenie:afrogenie@localhost:55432/afrogenie?schema=public
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:56379

# The guard's denylist is empty on purpose. `scripts/load-test-env.cjs` derives
# the allowlist from the URLs above, so a connection to anything that is not
# these two loopback containers fails closed. Never add a hostname here.
TEST_DB_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1
TEST_REDIS_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1
TEST_API_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1

# Defence in depth: the live development database, named so it can never be
# reached by a test run.
#
# `scripts/lib/db-host.cjs` protects every host by default, but that default is
# RELAXED for any host listed in TEST_DB_HOSTS above. Naming the real database
# here makes the protection explicit and unconditional, so an accidental
# `TEST_DB_HOSTS=...,-pooler...` edit fails closed instead of writing 8,721
# rows of real data to a throwaway test database. Hostnames are not secrets, so
# this file stays safe to commit.
#
# Added after the 2026-09-30 data-loss incident, in which every table in this
# database was rebuilt and emptied. See REMEDIATION-RESULTS.md 8.R1.
PRISMA_PROTECTED_HOSTS=ep-old-rice-ataoe41y-pooler.c-9.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech,ep-old-rice-ataoe41y.c-9.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech

# The HTTP API under test.
#
# Stage 7.7 removed the last test that used this: no test in the repo performs a
# network call to a separately-started API any more. They POSTed /auth/register
# and friends to whatever answered on this URL, which meant a developer running
# `npm run dev` alongside the suite could have their local (or, if misconfigured,
# real) database written to. A loopback URL is not proof of where that API's
# DATABASE_URL points, so the value is kept only as the runner's own allowlist
# input and is not a licence to send traffic at it. Coverage that needed an HTTP
# surface is now in-process (see the //SAFETY note in package.json).
TEST_API_URL=http://localhost:4010

# ─── Inert local placeholders (required by the zod schema in src/lib/env.ts) ─
JWT_SECRET=test-only-jwt-secret-not-used-in-production-0000000000
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=test-only-jwt-refresh-secret-not-used-in-prod-0000
TYPESENSE_HOST=localhost
TYPESENSE_PORT=9108
TYPESENSE_PROTOCOL=http
TYPESENSE_API_KEY=test-only-typesense-key
GEMINI_API_KEY=test-only-gemini-key

# Paystack — inert placeholders, NOT a real key.
#
# `paymentsAreConfigured()` in src/lib/env.ts is a pure truthiness check over
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY / PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY / PAYSTACK_CALLBACK_URL, so a
# placeholder satisfies it and every payment suite reaches the code under test.
# No request can leave the process: `stubPaystack` (test/paymentFixtures.ts)
# intercepts `fetch`, and the suites assert on signatures they compute from this
# same value, so a placeholder is functionally identical to a real key.
#
# These were ABSENT here until now, which meant the payment suites were not
# hermetic at all — they were silently reading the real `sk_test_` value out of a
# developer's `.env`. That is invisible on a laptop and fatal on a clean CI
# runner with no `.env`, so it is declared explicitly instead. See also
# THIRD_PARTY_KEYS_NEVER_REAL in scripts/lib/test-env.cjs, which forces every
# credential NOT named in this file to an empty string precisely so that `.env`
# can never reintroduce a live one.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=test-only-paystack-secret-key
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=test-only-paystack-public-key
PAYSTACK_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3000/buy-gt

# YOUTUBE_API_KEY is deliberately UNSET, matching .env.example and production.
#
# An earlier draft set it to a placeholder string. That was wrong twice over: a
# non-empty value flips `youtubeService.isConfigured()` to true, so the
# enrichment and admin match paths stop short-circuiting and issue real requests
# to youtube.googleapis.com with a bogus key. Tests then depended on a
# third-party 400 arriving fast enough. Leaving it unset means the "not
# configured" short-circuit is the default, and any test that genuinely needs
# YouTube stubs `fetch` (see test/phase4PlaybackRollout.test.ts). The schema
# marks this key optional, so nothing breaks.

# ─── Test-only behaviour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Workers are exercised explicitly by the job tests; the runner itself must not
# start background queues that would race those tests.
ENABLE_WORKERS=false

# Phase 4 playback rollout flag. OFF, matching .env.example and production.
# Tests that need the YouTube tier pin `env.FLAG_PLAYBACK_YOUTUBE = true` (and
# restore it), so the suite must not depend on an ambient value: a test that
# asserts "the flag is off" is only meaningful if the environment agrees, and a
# test that asserts "the flag is on" must say so itself.
FLAG_PLAYBACK_YOUTUBE=false
VITE_FLAG_PLAYBACK_YOUTUBE=false

# Never set ALLOW_PROD_TESTS here. The test runner refuses to start if it is
# present while the resolved hosts are not in the allowlist above.
